---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Height Converter - Feet, Inches, CM & Meters (Stature & Photo Sizing)"
  description="Convert height between centimeters, meters, feet, and inches. Includes quick cm-to-feet conversion tables, biometric BMI insights, and photo width and height sizing guidelines."
  category="General"
  calculatorName="Height Converter"
  slug="height-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'height converter',
    'height converter cm to feet',
    'height converter ft to cm',
    'height converter in cm',
    'height converter cm to feet inch',
    'height converter inch to cm',
    'height converter to feet',
    'height converter kg to cm',
    'height converter ft to m',
    'height converter mm to feet',
    'width and height converter',
    'photo width and height converter',
    'image width and height converter',
    'photo weight and height converter',
    'jpg width and height converter',
    'cm to height converter',
    'feet to cm',
    'meters to feet',
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Input Value & Unit -->
      <div>
        <label for="input-height-val" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Height Value
        </label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="input-height-val"
          value="175"
          step="any"
          class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-white"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <label for="select-height-unit" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          From Unit
        </label>
        <select
          id="select-height-unit"
          class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-white"
        >
          <option value="cm" selected>Centimeters (cm)</option>
          <option value="m">Meters (m)</option>
          <option value="inches">Inches (in)</option>
          <option value="feet">Decimal Feet (ft)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ACTION BUTTONS: CONVERT & CLEAR -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pt-1">
      <button
        type="button"
        id="btn-calc-height"
        class="flex-1 min-w-50 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-linear-to-r from-blue-600 to-indigo-600 hover:from-blue-700 hover:to-indigo-700 px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-500/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
      >
        <span>⚡ Convert Height</span>
        <span>→</span>
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        id="btn-clear-height"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-5 py-3.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 hover:text-red-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 dark:hover:bg-slate-700 dark:hover:text-red-400 transition cursor-pointer"
        title="Reset or Clear Input"
      >
        <span>🔄 Clear / Reset</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Conversion Results Grid -->
    <div id="results-card" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Feet & Inches Equivalent</span>
        <div id="res-ft-in" class="mt-1 text-3xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
          5' 8.9"
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4 text-xs">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/60 bg-white p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Centimeters</div>
          <div id="res-cm" class="mt-1 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">175 cm</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/60 bg-white p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Meters</div>
          <div id="res-m" class="mt-1 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1.75 m</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/60 bg-white p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Total Inches</div>
          <div id="res-in" class="mt-1 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">68.9 in</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/60 bg-white p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Decimal Feet</div>
          <div id="res-ft-dec" class="mt-1 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5.74 ft</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How Height Conversion Works Across Everyday Systems</h2>
    <p>
      You fill out an official visa document, passport application, or medical intake form, and suddenly you need your stature in centimeters when you only know your height as 5 feet 10 inches. Or perhaps you are reviewing clinical lab notes where stature is recorded strictly in meters.
    </p>
    <p>
      A dependable <strong>height converter</strong> bridges that divide instantly. Whether you need a quick <strong>height converter cm to feet</strong> calculation, a reliable <strong>height converter ft to cm</strong> reference, or want to check your exact <strong>height converter in cm</strong>, understanding the underlying math prevents errors on important paperwork.
    </p>

    <h3>The Arithmetic of Converting Feet and Inches to Centimeters</h3>
    <p>
      Converting between imperial and metric stature relies on a universal standard established in 1959. That treaty defined one international inch as exactly 2.54 centimeters.
    </p>
    <p>
      When using a <strong>height converter cm to feet inch</strong>, the conversion follows three simple steps:
    </p>
    <ol class="my-3 space-y-1.5 list-decimal pl-5">
      <li>Convert your feet into inches by multiplying by 12. For example, 5 feet equals 60 inches.</li>
      <li>Add any remaining inches. If you stand 5'9", add 9 to 60 to reach 69 total inches.</li>
      <li>Multiply your total inches by 2.54. In this case, 69 multiplied by 2.54 gives exactly 175.26 cm (or 1.75 meters).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The reverse calculation for a <strong>cm to height converter</strong> divides your centimeters by 2.54 to determine total inches. Dividing that result by 12 produces your whole feet, with the remainder representing inches. For smaller technical measurements, a <strong>height converter mm to feet</strong> divides millimeters by 304.8, while a <strong>height converter ft to m</strong> multiplies decimal feet by 0.3048.
    </p>

    <h3>Height Conversion Chart from Feet to Centimeters and Meters</h3>
    <p>
      Use this quick reference table to find common adult height equivalents between imperial feet, total inches, centimeters, and meters:
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
      <table class="min-w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <thead>
