            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">64 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">162.6 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.63 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">5' 6"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">66 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">167.6 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.68 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">5' 8"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">68 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">172.7 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.73 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">5' 10"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">70 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">177.8 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.78 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">6' 0"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">72 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">182.9 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.83 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">6' 2"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">74 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">188.0 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.88 m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">6' 4"</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">76 in</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">193.0 cm</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">1.93 m</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Why Height and Body Mass Connect in Health Screening</h3>
    <p>
      Many people searching for a <strong>height converter kg to cm</strong> are looking to evaluate their physical proportions. Medical screening formulas never analyze height in isolation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your standing height squared in meters forms the foundation of our <a href="/health/bmi-calculator/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">BMI calculator</a>. If you need to convert your body mass between pounds, kilograms, and stones before running your health score, our <a href="/general/weight-calculator/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">universal weight calculator</a> provides immediate conversions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Stature is also a key variable on our <a href="/health/body-fat-calculator/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">body fat percentage calculator</a>, which pairs height with waist circumference to estimate lean muscle mass without specialized hospital machinery. To evaluate pediatric development, parents can compare height percentiles against calendar milestones using our <a href="/general/age-calculator/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">chronological age calculator</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Digital Media: Photo Width and Height Sizing</h3>
    <p>
      Beyond physical human stature, people regularly search for a <strong>width and height converter</strong> or <strong>photo width and height converter</strong> to format passport pictures, visa submissions, and online job portal uploads.
    </p>
    <p>
      A digital <strong>image width and height converter</strong> translates physical millimeter or centimeter requirements into screen pixels based on resolution DPI (dots per inch). For example:
    </p>
    <ul class="my-3 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <li>A standard 3.5 cm × 4.5 cm passport photo printed at 300 DPI measures roughly 413 × 531 pixels.</li>
      <li>A 2 × 2 inch US visa photo printed at 300 DPI equals exactly 600 × 600 pixels.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Online portals frequently demand a specific <strong>photo weight and height converter</strong> solution, where you must match both physical dimensions and a maximum file weight (such as a <strong>jpg width and height converter</strong> output under 50 KB). You can resize dimensions directly with our <a href="/free-online-tools/image-resizer/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">online image resizer</a>, compress file size under strict upload limits using our <a href="/free-online-tools/image-compressor/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">image compressor</a>, or convert picture formats with our <a href="/pdf-tools/image-to-pdf/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">image to PDF converter</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>International Measurement Standards and References</h3>
    <p>
      All conversion equations on this platform follow dimensional standards defined by the National Institute of Standards and Technology (<a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/weights-and-measures" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">NIST Weights and Measures</a>). For broader dimensional conversions across distance, speed, area, and temperature units, explore our universal <a href="/general/unit-converter/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">unit converter</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          What is the 5'7" height?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          A height of 5 feet 7 inches equals 67 inches or 170.18 centimeters (1.70 meters). In everyday terms, 5'7" sits comfortably above the worldwide adult female average (about 5'3" or 160 cm) and slightly below the average male height in North America and Northern Europe (about 5'9" to 5'10").
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          What height is 5 ft 7 in cm?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          5 ft 7 in equals exactly 170.18 cm. To calculate this manually: multiply 5 feet by 12 to get 60 inches, add 7 inches to reach 67 inches total, then multiply 67 by 2.54 cm.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          How tall is 5'4" in cm?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          5 feet 4 inches equals exactly 162.56 centimeters (or 1.63 meters rounded). That corresponds to 64 total inches, which is near the exact median adult female height in the United States, Canada, and parts of Europe.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          What height is 5ft 2 in cm?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          5 feet 2 inches converts to exactly 157.48 centimeters (1.57 meters). It equals 62 total inches (5 × 12 + 2) multiplied by 2.54.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          How many centimeters is 5 feet 10 inches?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          5 feet 10 inches equals 70 inches total, which is exactly 177.8 cm (1.778 meters).
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          How do you convert centimeters to feet and inches manually?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Divide your centimeter measurement by 2.54 to find your stature in total inches. Then divide total inches by 12 to find whole feet, with the remainder representing inches. For example, 175 cm divided by 2.54 gives 68.89 inches, which equals 5 feet 8.89 inches.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
          What are standard photo width and height dimensions for official applications?
          <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Indian passport and exam portals typically mandate 3.5 cm width by 4.5 cm height (approx. 413 × 531 pixels at 300 DPI) under 50 KB. For US visas and passports, the requirement is 2 × 2 inches (51 mm × 51 mm, or 600 × 600 pixels). You can format images to these exact ratios using our <a href="/free-online-tools/image-resizer/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">image resizer</a> and <a href="/free-online-tools/passport-photo-maker/" class="font-medium text-blue-600 underline dark:text-blue-400">passport photo maker</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

<script is:inline>
  const heightVal = document.getElementById('input-height-val');
  const heightUnit = document.getElementById('select-height-unit');
  const resFtIn = document.getElementById('res-ft-in');
  const resCm = document.getElementById('res-cm');
  const resM = document.getElementById('res-m');
  const resIn = document.getElementById('res-in');
  const resFtDec = document.getElementById('res-ft-dec');

  function convert() {
    const rawVal = heightVal.value.trim();
    if (rawVal === '') {
      resFtIn.textContent = '0\' 0.0"';
      resCm.textContent = '0.0 cm';
      resM.textContent = '0.000 m';
      resIn.textContent = '0.0 in';
      resFtDec.textContent = '0.00 ft';
      try { document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('calculator:updated')); } catch (e) {}
      return;
    }

    const val = parseFloat(heightVal.value) || 0;
    const unit = heightUnit.value;

    let cm = 0;
    if (unit === 'cm') cm = val;
    else if (unit === 'm') cm = val * 100;
    else if (unit === 'inches') cm = val * 2.54;
    else if (unit === 'feet') cm = val * 30.48;

    const meters = (cm / 100).toFixed(3);
    const totalInches = (cm / 2.54);
    const ft = Math.floor(totalInches / 12);
    const inch = (totalInches % 12).toFixed(1);

    resFtIn.textContent = `${ft}' ${inch}"`;
    resCm.textContent = `${cm.toFixed(1)} cm`;
    resM.textContent = `${meters} m`;
    resIn.textContent = `${totalInches.toFixed(1)} in`;
    resFtDec.textContent = `${(totalInches / 12).toFixed(2)} ft`;

    try { document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('calculator:updated')); } catch (e) {}
  }

  const btnCalcHeight = document.getElementById('btn-calc-height');
  const btnClearHeight = document.getElementById('btn-clear-height');

  if (btnCalcHeight) {
    btnCalcHeight.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!heightVal.value) heightVal.value = '175';
      convert();
      const card = document.getElementById('results-card');
      if (card) card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      const orig = btnCalcHeight.innerHTML;
      btnCalcHeight.innerHTML = '<span>✅ Converted!</span>';
      setTimeout(() => { btnCalcHeight.innerHTML = orig; }, 1200);
    });
  }

  if (btnClearHeight) {
    btnClearHeight.addEventListener('click', () => {
      heightVal.value = '';
      convert();
      heightVal.focus();
      const orig = btnClearHeight.innerHTML;
      btnClearHeight.innerHTML = '<span>✓ Cleared</span>';
      setTimeout(() => { btnClearHeight.innerHTML = orig; }, 1000);
    });
  }

  heightVal.addEventListener('input', convert);
  heightUnit.addEventListener('change', convert);
  heightVal.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') {
      e.preventDefault();
      convert();
    }
  });
  convert();
</script>
